# Cell from playpick: mode=raid, boss=gorged (The Bloodgorged), spec=warlock:
# destruction, style=dodge, size=10, difficulty=normal, view=1280x800
# (desktop, mouse), save=fresh.
#
# Checked direction.md first. Hypothesis 1's Bloodgorged thread has two
# independently-confirmed mechanisms so far, both at 25-player: `fester`
# punishes a healer that never acts (idle, 25-heroic), and `gorge` punishes a
# body that never leaves melee range (melee's own blind steering, 25-normal).
# Neither has been read against a style that moves but never attacks, and
# neither has been read at 10-player at all -- every Bloodgorged reading on
# this line so far is 25-heroic or 25-normal. playbot.ts's own dodge branch
# only steers away from danger and never presses an ability (confirmed in
# 2026-10-02-18.play's own header), so this is the cleanest test yet of
# whether staying out of melee range (dodge's whole job) sidesteps `gorge`
# the way idle's healing-starvation sidesteps nothing -- on a boss, a size and
# a role (ranged dps) this thread has not yet combined.
open #b=gorged&s=10&h=0
tap class:warlock:destruction
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot opening
play dodge 150
state
shot ending
says
bill
